# Placeholders for every in-process module's required configuration, so all of them load in the boot check
# (scripts/smoke.sh). None is a real credential. Hosts end in .invalid (RFC 2606): DNS refuses them, so nothing
# leaves the runner even when a module reaches out at start-up (calendar's refresh job does).
#
# A new module with required keys fails the boot check until its placeholders are added here.
# Never add ICLOUD_USERNAME or ICLOUD_APP_PASSWORD: the CalDAV client only talks to the real *.icloud.com, so fake
# credentials would reach Apple. INTAKE_URL and INTAKE_KEY are enough for the calendar module to load.
# No GEMINI_API_KEY either: the check starts no session.
JELLYFIN_URL=http://jellyfin.invalid
JELLYFIN_API_KEY=placeholder
TOMTOM_API_KEY=placeholder
HA_URL=http://homeassistant.invalid
HA_TOKEN=placeholder
INTAKE_URL=http://intake.invalid/out
INTAKE_KEY=placeholder
